In `store.js.es6` `_hydrateEmbedded`, the new plural branch maps each id to `_lookupSubType(...)`:
```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(function(id) {
  return self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root);
});
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
delete obj[k];
```
Unlike the singular branch (which only assigns `obj[subType] = hydrated` when `hydrated` is truthy), this always assigns the array and always deletes the original `*_ids` key. If `_lookupSubType` fails for an id (returns `undefined`/`null`), the resulting array will contain `undefined` entries, and the original ids are lost—m

The diff explicitly adds an adapter for the `embedding` model at `app/assets/javascripts/admin/adapters/embedding.js.es6`:

```js
export default RestAdapter.extend({
  pathFor() {
    return "/admin/customize/embedding";
  }
});
```

So `this.store.find('embedding')` (added in `admin/routes/admin-embedding.js.es6`) will not request `/embeddings`; it will use the adapter’s `pathFor()` and hit `/admin/customize/embedding`, which is also added to Rails routes (`get "customize/embedding" => "embedding#show"`).
